  [PASS] C1 THE THEOREM.  Every single-radius statistic in which the extra measured inputs enter multiplicatively must be shown to be the RAR reparametrised -- the shuffle must not move it at all.  A PASS here is a NEGATIVE result for the hunt: it means this whole class of candidate cannot contain a second law   (10 of 12 candidates are inside the closure: ['A', 'B', 'C', 'D', 'E', 'F', 'G', 'H', 'I', 'J'])
  [PASS] C2 THE TEST MUST NOT BE VACUOUS.  The two deliberate escapes -- a two-radius statistic and a non-multiplicative one -- must MOVE under the same shuffle, or the test detects nothing   (escapes that moved: ['K', 'L'])

